                <pb facs="0168" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg64"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11, 1890</date>.
                        (Received August 11.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Mizner informs Mr. Blaine that the Salvadorian Government, in accordance with
                    our minister’s demand, hoisted the flag of the United States over our consulate
                    in San Salvador, firing a salute of twenty-one <pb facs="0169" n="65"
                        xml:id="pg65"/> guns; reinstated the consul in his office and guarantied his
                    rights. He reports the satisfactory conclusion of the incident by an adequate
                    letter of apology from the Salvadorian minister for foreign affairs.</p>
            </div>
